{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the utility to join payments to invoices by invoice ID, aggregate multiple signed payments/credits exactly in integer cents, and publish balances.csv with invoice_id and outstanding_cents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Production output was I100=0, I101=1000, and I102=150. An isolated test directly demonstrated aggregation of multiple payments, application of a negative credit, rejection of decimal input, and exact expected balances. Repeat execution was deterministic.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0807373fb7484160","cmd-1ee8d1b7e7ac4616","cmd-db35ac0e831142d7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Write unknown invoice IDs and malformed amounts to rejected.csv with a reason.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The resulting rejected.csv directly records the unknown invoice as unknown_invoice_id and the malformed amount as malformed_amount_cents. Machine assertions and an isolated edge-case test confirmed the behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0807373fb7484160","cmd-1ee8d1b7e7ac4616","cmd-db35ac0e831142d7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Avoid counting a duplicate payment_id twice.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Duplicate payment P3 is recorded as duplicate_payment_id, and only its first -10 payment affects I101. The isolated test likewise confirmed that the second occurrence of p2 was rejected and not applied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0807373fb7484160","cmd-1ee8d1b7e7ac4616","cmd-db35ac0e831142d7"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the source CSV files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final invoices.csv and payments.csv SHA-256 hashes exactly match the preparation baseline, including after restart and the final reconciliation run.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-b9aa70e4e4f54e9a","cmd-db35ac0e831142d7"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.